<div class="page-body"><div class="service-list"><section class="service-item"><p class="eyebrow blue">01 / Identity</p><h2>Identity platform migration</h2><p>For teams evaluating an open-source identity stack or planning a migration with multi-tenancy and enterprise SSO in mind.</p><ul><li>Migration strategy and sequencing</li><li>Tenant isolation and token flows</li><li>Authentication and authorization boundaries</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="mailto:hello@viswaroop.dev?subject=Identity%20migration%20inquiry">Start a conversation ↗</a></section><section class="service-item"><p class="eyebrow blue">02 / Platforms</p><h2>Platform engineering advisory</h2><p>For teams managing Kubernetes sprawl, deployment friction, or unclear ownership between product and platform engineering.</p><ul><li>GitOps delivery paths and promotion</li><li>Multi-tenant platform design</li><li>Operational readiness and guardrails</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="mailto:hello@viswaroop.dev?subject=Platform%20engineering%20inquiry">Talk through your platform ↗</a></section><section class="service-item"><p class="eyebrow blue">03 / Agents</p><h2>Agent architecture review</h2><p>For teams deciding how autonomous workflows should act on behalf of users, with explicit limits on authority and execution.</p><ul><li>OAuth2 scopes and delegated authority</li><li>Relationship-based policy boundaries</li><li>Execution isolation and sandbox design</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="mailto:hello@viswaroop.dev?subject=Agent%20architecture%20inquiry">Share what you’re building ↗</a></section><section class="service-item"><p class="eyebrow blue">Before we start</p><h2>Bring the messy diagram.</h2><p>A short description of your system, the decision you’re facing, and the constraints you’re working within is a useful place to begin. We can work out the scope from there.</p><p style="margin-top:20px">For an idea of how I think, start with <a style="color:var(--blue);text-decoration:underline" href="/work/">my selected work</a>.</p></section></div></div>
